### 4. Deploy Workloads on Destination Cluster

> **Applies to:** SIT, NFT, PRP, PRD, PRX

Use the release branch identified in the [Release Branch for Main Workload Deployments](#release-branch-for-main-workload-deployments) prerequisite step.

**Deploy workloads (main stacks):**

- **Pipeline:** [cpp-aks-deploy](https://dev.azure.com/hmcts-cpp/cpp-apps/_build?definitionId=333)

This pipeline deploys the following namespaces per stack:

- `ns-<env>-ccm-<stack>`
- `ns-<env>-idam-<stack>`
- `ns-<env>-cdns-<stack>`
- `ns-<env>-web-<stack>`

Parameters:
- `Environment:` your target environment (SIT/DEV/STE etc)
- `Stack:` your stack (\<env>ccm01 for non DEV/STE environments)
- `Cluster:` target cluster in full (e.g. K8-SIT-CS01-CL01)
- `CPP Pipeline Branch:` use value found in [Release Branch for Main Workload Deployments](#release-branch-for-main-workload-deployments) step above
- ensure `deploy-service` & `create_replica_configmap` are checked


**Deploy Alfapp workloads:**

For `ns-<env>-alfapp-<stack>` namespaces, use a separate pipeline:

- **Pipeline:** [cpp-alfresco-deploy](https://dev.azure.com/hmcts-cpp/cpp-apps/_build?definitionId=181)

Parameters:

- deploy from `release/1.35` branch

**Deploy Results Definition workloads:**

For `ns-<env>-rd-<stack>` namespaces, use this pipeline:

- **Pipeline:** [results-definition-pipeline](https://dev.azure.com/hmcts-cpp/cpp-apps/_build?definitionId=586)

Parameters:

- deploy from `main` branch
- leave imageTag as default

**Deploy API Marketplace workloads:**

For `ns-<env>-amp-<stack>` namespaces, use this pipeline:

- **Pipeline:** [cp-vp-aks-deploy](https://dev.azure.com/hmcts-cpp/cpp-apps/_build?definitionId=434)

Parameters:

- use `env/<env>` for branch (check branches that this exists first)
- `Environment:` <env> (e.g. sit/dev/ste etc)
- `CP Backend Target Environment:` <env>ccm01 (or another stack if DEV/STE)
- `Stack:` \<env>amp01 (e.g. sitamp01)
- `Cluster:` target cluster in full (e.g. K8-SIT-CS01-CL01)

For detailed instructions on deploying to AKS, refer to the [Deploy to AKS](https://tools.hmcts.net/confluence/spaces/EI/pages/1525460437/Deploy+to+AKS) guide.


